1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,600
[Episode 14]

3
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:09,870
We're sorry to have disturbed you.

4
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:11,120
Goodbye.

5
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:11,920
Thank you.

6
00:01:16,310 --> 00:01:17,070
Oh, sorry.

7
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:17,870
Officer Han.

8
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,280
That area is off-limits.

9
00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:22,680
What's over there?

10
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:24,640
The genetics lab.

11
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:27,640
It involves trade secrets,

12
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:28,870
so we can't let visitors in.

13
00:01:29,310 --> 00:01:30,310
Sorry about that.

14
00:01:30,310 --> 00:01:30,870
I understand.

15
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:31,710
Sorry.
Mm.

16
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:32,920
This way.

17
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:34,040
Okay.
No need to see us out.

18
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:48,480
Have you noticed how today's tycoons

19
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,070
all seem so refined?

20
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:54,150
He once made a fortune illegally,

21
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:57,120
but now styles himself
as a successful businessman.

22
00:01:57,430 --> 00:01:58,510
I don't believe him for a second.

23
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,760
Still,

24
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,430
he gave nothing away today.

25
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,280
Hey.

26
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:06,310
Do you smell that?

27
00:02:06,310 --> 00:02:08,710
It smells like hospital disinfectant.

28
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:12,710
No.

29
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:14,080
Mm.

30
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:15,960
Maybe it's because I've feared needles
since childhood.

31
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:18,560
Whenever I smell this odor,

32
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:20,240
it makes my skin crawl.

33
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:22,520
Mm.
Let's go.

34
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:34,360
Sorry.

35
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,120
Watch where you're going!

36
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,310
Forget it.

37
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:40,320
[Ibuprofen Granules]

38
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:25,310
Wait.

39
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,560
Delivering medicine to a ward?

40
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:33,510
Drop this file at the director's office.

41
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:34,950
Okay.

42
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:44,430
Get in here and help!

43
00:04:46,070 --> 00:04:47,560
Blood pressure cuff and hemostat.
Now!

44
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:54,160
What's going on?

45
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:56,630
Halfway through egg retrieval,
she forgot to apply her anesthetic.

46
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:58,830
Stop! Stop!

47
00:04:58,950 --> 00:05:00,630
Stop!
Go get the anesthetic!

48
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:01,040
Help me.

49
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:02,270
Get the anesthetic!

50
00:05:02,270 --> 00:05:04,750
There's no time to start over.
Tough it out.

51
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:09,830
What are you doing?

52
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:11,070
Press harder.

53
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,240
You forgot the anesthetic.
Who's to blame?

54
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:25,160
It hurts, doctor.

55
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:33,160
Don't just stand there!

56
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:34,160
Come help!

57
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:36,750
Are you new?

58
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:38,000
Which department are you from?

59
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:38,750
I...

60
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:40,750
I...

61
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:43,160
Grab her!

62
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:45,680
Ah!

63
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,480
Don't move!

64
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,190
What you're doing

65
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:20,600
leaves no room for negotiation.

66
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:22,750
Why go so far?

67
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,720
You deceived me first.

68
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:28,600
Hey, don't make false accusations.

69
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:30,310
We agreed that

70
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,510
you'd get paid after giving birth.

71
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,800
Who knew you'd miscarry?

72
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:37,190
Your failure to deliver a baby

73
00:06:37,190 --> 00:06:38,310
isn't my problem.

74
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,870
You're a college student.

75
00:06:41,870 --> 00:06:42,830
Surely

76
00:06:43,390 --> 00:06:44,560
you understand something this simple.

77
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,360
You never told me

78
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:49,270
I'd be caged like an animal,

79
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:51,040
or that after I miscarried,

80
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:53,000
you'd simply send me away.

81
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:53,750
Shh.

82
00:06:54,270 --> 00:06:56,510
What does that have to do with our deal?

83
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,800
Deliver the baby, get paid.

84
00:06:58,800 --> 00:06:59,920
It's that simple.

85
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:02,750
Ever heard of honoring a contract,
college girl?

86
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:07,800
Don't look at me like that.

87
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:13,750
Do you know how much surrogacy costs?

88
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:17,000
Only for us to end up with nothing?

89
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,270
I should be demanding money from you.

90
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:23,600
My body is ruined too!

91
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,510
What?
Regretting it?

92
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,270
Mm.

93
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:33,310
Since being alive only makes you suffer,

94
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:37,190
why not put yourself in my hands?

95
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:52,750
The police found this place.

96
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:55,480
Relax.

97
00:07:56,070 --> 00:07:56,870
They only asked a few questions.

98
00:07:57,390 --> 00:07:57,630
Hmph.

99
00:07:59,190 --> 00:08:01,950
They found the body dump site.

100
00:08:02,390 --> 00:08:05,600
Your men didn't clean up properly.

101
00:08:06,950 --> 00:08:08,190
You even kept me in the dark.

102
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:09,920
I only just found out.

103
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:14,190
But a few bodies

104
00:08:14,270 --> 00:08:15,920
won't tell them much.

105
00:08:16,070 --> 00:08:16,870
Right.

106
00:08:17,310 --> 00:08:18,510
They probably won't find much.

107
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,190
But they've come knocking.

108
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:24,360
Who knows what you've told them?

109
00:08:35,750 --> 00:08:38,480
It's time to move the pawns you planted.

110
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:42,790
Otherwise,
that Han guy will avenge his sister

111
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:44,200
and keep digging to the bitter end.

112
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:49,270
You want me to go after a cop?

113
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,550
This is the last time you question me.

114
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,390
There won't be another.

115
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,150
Huh?

116
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:04,600
Also,

117
00:09:05,390 --> 00:09:06,790
that girl from earlier...

118
00:09:08,030 --> 00:09:09,200
Hand her over to me.

119
00:09:18,910 --> 00:09:19,600
Sorry to keep you waiting.

120
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:20,550
Sorry.

121
00:09:21,670 --> 00:09:23,200
I should be the one apologizing.

122
00:09:23,750 --> 00:09:25,670
I always take things from you for free.

123
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,200
We're friends.
Don't mention it.

124
00:09:28,790 --> 00:09:31,150
Any news on your sister?

125
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:36,720
Nothing yet.

126
00:09:38,510 --> 00:09:39,390
Sometimes

127
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:43,480
no news is good news.

128
00:09:45,550 --> 00:09:47,870
From a psychological perspective,

129
00:09:47,870 --> 00:09:50,870
we often understand sibling bonds
through parent-child dynamics.

130
00:09:53,390 --> 00:09:54,200
Yes.

131
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,200
Especially for someone like me.

132
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:58,000
My parents died when I was young,

133
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,080
so my sister

134
00:09:59,750 --> 00:10:00,870
naturally

135
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:03,200
took on the role of a mother.

136
00:10:03,510 --> 00:10:03,870
Yes.

137
00:10:04,550 --> 00:10:06,360
That was crucial in shaping

138
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:08,150
your character and emotions.

139
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:11,360
Over time, that creates dependency.

140
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,510
Once that bond is gone,

141
00:10:13,510 --> 00:10:15,000
you feel lost.

142
00:10:15,510 --> 00:10:16,960
Now that you're aware of the problem,

143
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:19,150
adjust one step at a time.

144
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:21,320
You're your own person.

145
00:10:21,670 --> 00:10:23,150
You can't keep living in the past.

146
00:10:26,910 --> 00:10:27,720
Xiaowei.

147
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:29,960
You're back.

148
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:31,870
This is the friend I told you about,

149
00:10:31,870 --> 00:10:32,510
Han Ning.

150
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:40,790
Sorry.
My brother has been ill for years,

151
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:42,320
so he's a little...

152
00:10:42,550 --> 00:10:44,000
It's okay.
I understand.

153
00:10:45,510 --> 00:10:47,360
Compared with all he's suffered,

154
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,720
my problems are nothing.

155
00:10:49,550 --> 00:10:51,120
As long as my brother gets well,

156
00:10:51,910 --> 00:10:53,120
I'll do anything.

157
00:11:04,270 --> 00:11:05,870
Bye.
Remember to take your medicine.

158
00:11:05,910 --> 00:11:06,390
Okay.

159
00:11:06,390 --> 00:11:07,200
See you next time.

160
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:28,550
I think the police have new leads

161
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,750
about what happened seven years ago:

162
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,390
Han Shuang's disappearance.

163
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,990
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

164
00:12:12,990 --> 00:12:14,930
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

165
00:12:14,930 --> 00:12:16,840
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

166
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:18,650
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

167
00:12:18,650 --> 00:12:20,990
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

168
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:23,410
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

169
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:28,460
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

170
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:30,360
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

171
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:32,300
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

172
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:34,430
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

173
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:36,440
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

174
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,600
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

175
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:45,670
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

176
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:49,040
♪Why is that child crying?♪

177
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:51,740
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

178
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:53,360
♪Means I've grown up♪

179
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:56,510
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

180
00:12:56,510 --> 00:13:00,000
♪The wound still aches♪

181
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:04,760
♪Like a biting winter♪

182
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:08,020
♪But a spark still glows♪

